A||||14||Raydar||Had close call today.||||1||
Z||000000||Raydar||05-05-2001||12:20 AM||||Well, I had just left work. On my way to get gas before I headed home. Taking a road that I don't frequently take, due to a huge concert having many of the roads near my building closed. Not in a particular hurry. Watching the folks as I drive down the street. See a woman crossing the street about 65-75 feet in front of me. Off to my right, about 35-40 feet in front of me, is a child about 8 or 10, standing next to a parked car, watching the other woman. <BR>I'm thinking to myself "She's GOT to look. She's NOT gonna run out in front of me."<BR>Well, she didn't. And she did. <BR>Slammed on my brakes and skidded to a stop.  When she heard the skid, she looked up and stopped, too. By the time we were both stopped, there was only about a foot and a half between the headlight of my truck, and where she was standing.<BR>I'm just thankful that I was paying attention, and was able to perceive what was going to happen. If I hadn't stopped, I surely would have hit her. <BR>God was watching out for the both of us.      <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cheever2||05-05-2001||02:10 AM||||I bet you'll be replaying that in your mind a few thousand times.  <P>Gotta watch for everything and expect the worst.<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000002||Wolfhound||05-05-2001||05:42 AM||||Radar, A couple of weeks ago I was on a two lane county road running about 50. I came up on a car stopped, coming out of a driveway with about a foot of the front end out in the road. It was about six AM and the sun was just coming up. The car had just been cranked and there was condensation coming from the exaust and the windows were still fogged. I wasn't sure the driver could see me so I slowed to about 30. I approached watching the car and a lady (the cars driver) stepped away from her mailbox across the street right in front of me, going through her mail. I dodged her and I came close enough that she dropped her mail in the road. It took most of the day for me to get over that to the point I could function normally. Scarry,I had been watching the wrong thing.<BR>Coy ||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||05-05-2001||01:40 PM||||Just last night, around 3am, when lots of bars are starting to let out, we're cruising south on highway 17 at about 50-55 on the left lane. We see a white pickup cut across 17 north on the left, and drive slowly in the median lane, we figured he was going to wait for us to pass, and turn onto the left lane. He sure didn't! We were about a car-length behind him when he cut out in front of us! We slammed on the brakes, only locked them up for a second, when we were about a foot or two from hitting him, he cut immediately right and made a right turn. <BR>We turned around, hit the blue lights and siren, well, you can guess what happened next! "have you been drinking tonight?" LOL ||||reg||1
